flags declares one flag of every kind and prints what the parser made of them.

The count flag is persistent, so -v, -vvv and --verbose=3 work on either side
of the subcommand.

Usage:
  flags [flags]
  flags [command]

Available Commands:
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  echo        Print the inherited count
  help        Help about any command

Flags:
  -e, --emit llvm|obj     what to emit (default "llvm")
  -x, --exclude strings   names to skip
  -h, --help              help for flags
  -r, --rate float        rate to apply (default 1.5)
  -t, --tag strings       tags to attach (default [a,b])
  -v, --verbose           verbosity, repeatable

Use "flags [command] --help" for more information about a command.
